        "name": "AlphaSignal"
      }
    },
    {
      "title": "TabFM",
      "url": "https://research.google/blog/introducing-tabfm-a-zero-shot-foundation-model-for-tabular-data/",
      "summary": "by Google Research uses an alternating row and column attention mechanism to score new query rows based on context examples. Trained entirely on synthetic datasets, TabFM encodes strong inductive biases while avoiding data privacy issues.",
      "published_at": "2026-07-26T14:32:06Z",
      "_source": {
        "from_address": "news@alphasignal.ai",
        "section": "newsletters",
        "topic": "research",
        "emoji": "📧",
        "name": "AlphaSignal"
      }
    },
    {
      "title": "via GitHub",
      "url": "https://github.com/google-research/tabfm",
      "summary": "TabFM is open-source and accessible with JAX and PyTorch backends under the Apache 2.0 license (it can be used for commercial applications). Google is also integrating TabFM natively into BigQuery. Soon, data analysts will be able to run zero-shot predictions directly in their data warehouse without building ML models.",
      "published_at": "2026-07-26T14:32:06Z",
      "_source": {
        "from_address": "news@alphasignal.ai",
        "section": "newsletters",
        "topic": "research",
        "emoji": "📧",
        "name": "AlphaSignal"
      }
    },
    {
      "title": "KumoRFM by Nvidia",
      "url": "https://docs.nvidia.com/sdgm/rfm/introduction",
      "summary": "moves beyond single tables by modeling relational data as graphs of interconnected tables. It predicts outcomes across complex enterprise schemas without requiring developers to flatten multiple databases into a massive CSV file.",
      "published_at": "2026-07-26T14:32:06Z",
      "_source": {
        "from_address": "news@alphasignal.ai",
        "section": "newsletters",
        "topic": "research",
        "emoji": "📧",
        "name": "AlphaSignal"
      }
    },
    {
      "title": "TabPFN",
      "url": "https://priorlabs.ai/tabpfn",
      "summary": "by Prior Labs pioneered this space with Prior-Data Fitted Networks. It treats tabular prediction as a completion problem, guessing the missing column based on strong mathematical priors baked in during synthetic pre-training.",
      "published_at": "2026-07-26T14:32:06Z",
      "_source": {
        "from_address": "news@alphasignal.ai",
        "section": "newsletters",
        "topic": "research",
        "emoji": "📧",
        "name": "AlphaSignal"
      }
    },
    {
      "title": "highly cited Nature paper",
      "url": "https://www.nature.com/articles/s41586-024-08328-6",
      "summary": "Backed by a , TabPFN is highly accessible for developers. It can be used as a fully managed cloud-based service via the Prior Labs API or downloaded locally as an . (It has a modified Apache 2.0 license that requires you to prominently display Prior Labs on your product.)",
